      "expected": "With no backup battery present, the STM32 backup-domain supply VBAT should normally be connected to VDD/VCC so the backup domain is powered and the power pin is not floating.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "netlist", "quote": "(net (code \"65\") (name \"unconnected-(U1-VBAT-Pad1)\") (node (ref \"U1\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"VBAT\") (pintype \"power_in+no_connect\"))"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "no battery, regulator, or USB part appears anywhere"}
      ],
      "impact": "The MCU backup-domain/RTC supply is unpowered and a power input is floating; this may cause ERC/design-rule issues and loss of backup-domain functionality, though main MCU operation may still continue.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The netlist mostly matches the described topology despite reference renumbering, but it leaves two power input pins floating: the SSD1306 VCC pin is only bypassed to GND and not connected to VCC, and the STM32 VBAT pin is marked no_connect."
}

